From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tonrakun <tonrakun@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:52:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Kodama: fix bucket collisions of chunk coordinate keys

License: GPL-3.0

The coordinate keys of ConcurrentHashMap returned (int) HashCommon.mix(key).
The low bits of that value xor its next 16 bits, and the spread of
ConcurrentHashMap xors them again, so the bucket index only depended on
chunkX: 3600 chunks around the origin used 60 of 8192 buckets, each a tree
bin of 60 entries. Folding the high half in spreads them over 2956 buckets.
ChunkHolderManager ticket lookups were 3-9% of the main thread with 20 bots.

diff --git a/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/concurrentutil/lock/ReentrantAreaLock.java b/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/concurrentutil/lock/ReentrantAreaLock.java
index 4fd9a0cd8f1e6ae1a97e963dc7731a80bc6fac5b..ff09f54c85266104bce4bc52186ee1d25f11b05f 100644
--- a/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/concurrentutil/lock/ReentrantAreaLock.java
+++ b/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/concurrentutil/lock/ReentrantAreaLock.java
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@ public final class ReentrantAreaLock {
 
         @Override
         public int hashCode() {
-            return (int)HashCommon.mix(this.key);
+            return HashCommon.long2int(HashCommon.mix(this.key)); // Kodama - with a plain (int) cast the spread of ConcurrentHashMap cancels the mix and buckets only by chunkX
         }
 
         @Override
